link, YAML/template and consistency checks, not claims of application E2E certification.

Build and validation coordination: use one heavy Cargo invocation per checkout at a time, and inspect existing jobs before starting another. A per-command `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS` limit does not bound the total memory of several concurrent Cargo processes. Use isolated worktrees for parallel edits and preserve other sessions' jobs; never terminate another project's work or delete active/shared caches. Finish related source edits before final validation, record the covered source fingerprint, and reject final-source certification when that input changes during the run. Run final compiler/test checks again after a repair; a prior binary or an interrupted Runner job is not evidence for new source. Read `docs/research/native_build_measurements_2026-09-19.md`: ten-minute core backend compilation, thirty-minute